WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.460
Is this an earthquake?

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:13.590
This must be...

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.840
Is this it?

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.260
Did he succeed?

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.080
NATIONAL ROUTE 246

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.080
<i>Disaster Control Headquarters here.</i>

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.340
<i>Officer Izumi,
can you confirm the situation?</i>

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.260
The city...

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:56.180
<i>It's not a wasteland anymore.
The Tokyo skyline is back.</i>

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:04.890
<i>You did it, Daisuke.</i>

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.460
Did that kid do this?

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:58.010
Yes. He did it.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.850
-Yes!
-Yes!

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:10.230
Lu!

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.770
Gai! Marimari!

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:16.900
He did it! Daisuke did it!
He returned Shibuya!

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.820
From above, I could clearly see
the rest of Tokyo.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:20.740
Right.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.780
<i>Daisuke really protected all of us.</i>

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.030
Yes.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.700
He finally did.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:28.830
-Where's Daisuke?
-What?

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:32.750
Don't tell me
that he was left behind in the future.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.290
No way.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:37.880
What is that?

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.380
Keisaku?

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:42.840
Keisaku!

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.340
Keisaku!

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:47.140
Gai, Lu, Marimari.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:49.310
I'm back.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.140
Keisaku, isn't Daisuke with you?

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.060
Daisuke?

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:57.400
That's right. He succeeded in destroying
the quantum brain at the Revisions' base.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:00.030
We returned, thanks to him.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:01.400
Daisuke promised that he--

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:02.990
What are you talking about?

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:06.320
Daisuke died in that kidnapping
seven years ago.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:07.370
What?

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:08.700
Keisaku?

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.290
What are you talking about?

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:12.540
Daisuke is gone.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.710
That's the true flow of history
in this timeline.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.970
<i>Was that Keisaku or Nicholas?</i>

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:25.890
<i>Either way, I have to get Keisaku back.</i>

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.100
<i>I have to get my best friend back.</i>

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:32.930
Where am I?

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:38.060
The boy who disappeared
is Keisaku Asano, age ten.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.980
He came here from Tokyo
for summer vacation.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:43.490
The kidnapper hasn't contacted us.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:44.780
However, since midday,

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:48.330
several residents reported seeing
an unfamiliar woman around.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.830
<i>-It was Keisaku who was kidnapped?</i>
-Right. At the festival.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:52.160
Not me?

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.080
Naturally, AHRV will try
to kill Keisaku Asano

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:58.340
who is a part of me.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:01.420
<i>Is Milo really going to...</i>

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:03.050
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:06.760
What should we do?

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:08.760
Daisuke.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:29.450
What? Is this kid me?

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:30.700
Who are you?

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:32.370
He looks suspicious!

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:35.290
I'm from the special police unit.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:38.710
I've been dispatched on
a top-secret mission to rescue Keisaku.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:42.090
Just look at me.
Pretty cool outfit, right?

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:46.010
You know, I think I've seen you on TV.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:50.260
Are you sure we can trust this guy?

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:52.060
He might just be a weird guy.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:54.850
But he said that he's a policeman.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:57.690
<i>What am I supposed to do now?</i>

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:01.520
<i>Without a String Puppet,
how am I supposed to fight Nicholas?</i>

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:05.820
<i>If everyone else was here
at a time like this...</i>

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:07.780
Hey.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.820
What is it, Lu?

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:12.740
Why are you crying?

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:13.700
What?

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:16.160
I'm not crying.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:19.170
Pull yourself together, Mr. Policeman.

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:23.750
So, you're all good friends, right?

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:24.920
Yes.

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:28.760
Then, no matter what happens
in the future,

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:32.100
I want you to believe Daisuke.

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:34.310
What? Well, sure. I will.

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:35.720
You won't forget, right?

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:36.770
I won't!

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:38.310
Lu! Hurry up!

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.400
We have to save Keisaku!

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:42.190
I know!

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:48.320
Do I have no other choice

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.070
than to accomplish this mission?

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:55.990
Who are you?

00:06:57.580 --> 00:06:58.750
Keisaku!

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:00.120
Daisuke?

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:02.040
What? Me?

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:03.080
-Keisaku!
-Keisaku!

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:04.540
Hey, you guys!

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:07.380
How the heck did you get to this time?

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.170
What happened to Shibuya?

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:12.390
Who cares about that?
Don't you dare do anything stupid!

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:16.890
Milo, if you kill Keisaku,
would that really help AHRV?

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:20.640
Can killing a single child
really save humanity?

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:23.360
I don't know, but...

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.190
this is all I can...

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.320
Humans confined by time are so pitiful.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:31.070
I was once like that.

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:32.740
Why, you!

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:33.820
Keisaku?

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:35.280
You're alive?

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:37.490
Milo, that's Nicholas.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:39.330
He has possessed Keisaku's body.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:40.710
He has possessed it?

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:42.620
I merged with it.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:45.710
You'd better not kill that boy.

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:50.800
If you do, I'll kill this boy Daisuke.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:51.800
Help me.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:54.050
-Daisuke!
-Let Daisuke go!

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.310
Hey, don't you think this is crazy?

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:59.060
What?

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:01.140
I thought you were totally strong.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:02.940
Why are you going to such trouble?

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:06.440
Wonderful!
You're quite intelligent, Daisuke.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:10.150
You're right. I am everywhere,
and I can go anywhere.

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:13.530
However, when I'm
in different places simultaneously,

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:16.070
my power becomes divided.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:17.410
Can you understand that?

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:21.620
I am a being
that exists outside the concept of time.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:24.580
-I am immortal.
-Keisaku?

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:26.380
How ironic.

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.050
Originally, it was supposed to be
Chiharu's or Mukyu's name

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:32.300
that would last forever.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.050
That fake doggy.

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:45.100
<i>If his power is divided,
then now is my chance.</i>

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:47.110
The three of you, get inside the shed.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.360
Okay.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.150
Milo.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:53.780
Don't be AHRV's pawn anymore.

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:55.660
"Protect everyone."

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:57.990
That's my destiny, right?

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:04.080
This time, AHRV's prediction of the future
was wrong from the start.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:09.460
In that prediction, I'm not
an important person to AHRV, right?

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.670
What? You knew?

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:19.680
Even so, Daisuke,

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:25.100
<i>you were a central figure
in the battle in 2388.</i>

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:29.230
And now, both you and I are here.

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:35.320
Daisuke, you defied destiny
and ended up here in this time.

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:38.620
I will bet on the possibilities
that are born from that!

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:48.920
I told you.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:51.460
Daisuke died back then.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:55.590
Come on.
Let's hurry and report to Ms. Izumi, Gai.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:57.510
Oh, okay.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:09:59.640
That's right.

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:02.100
Daisuke is gone, right?

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:04.430
That's right.

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:06.480
<i>Milo should have died back then.</i>

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:09.730
Forget it. We've finally returned.

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:10.860
Didn't I tell you?

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:13.570
I'm starving!

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:16.650
This might be the first time
we can eat our fill in a while.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:20.240
That's right.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.240
Hurry up and release Keisaku.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:28.460
If you don't,
I'll get rid of little Daisuke,

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:29.830
Poor boy.

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:33.460
You can't kill Keisaku.

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:35.760
Then, this is the only thing to do.

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:39.130
Okay, release that boy, Nicholas!

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:41.890
Daisuke!

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:46.060
Sorry to break my promise.

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:47.520
Daisuke!

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:53.570
Yes!

00:10:57.150 --> 00:11:00.530
What's with you, Daisuke?
Quit kidding around.

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:04.280
We're best friends, right?

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:10.120
Hold on!

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:14.790
Hey, Daisuke isn't dead!

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.300
I remember now!

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.550
<i>That guy told me during the kidnapping</i>

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:22.260
<i>to believe Daisuke and not to forget.</i>

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:24.180
That was probably Daisuke!

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:27.020
Oh, that's right. He's alive.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:28.730
Why...

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:30.600
<i>Why did I think that he died?</i>

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:32.770
<i>That's right.</i>

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:37.570
Daisuke went to the Revisions' base
all by himself.

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:40.610
Are everyone's scrambled memories

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:43.910
related to what you said, Keisaku?

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:54.380
Are you all right?

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:56.130
Yes.

00:11:58.630 --> 00:11:59.840
How are the kids?

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:00.880
They are fine.

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:03.510
Thank goodness.

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:07.180
Not again.

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:09.970
What a pain this is, poor boy.

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:14.770
Unfortunately, it seems
that our destinies are intertwined.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:19.230
How come you're alive?

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:20.820
How come?

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:25.160
Because I'm everywhere
outside the flow of time.

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:26.370
That's impossible.

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:28.700
Actually, Daisuke,

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:31.540
before coming here, at different times,

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:34.370
<i>I've tried several times to kill you.</i>

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:39.380
But like what happened just now,
someone interferes or I lose you.

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.260
It always doesn't go well.

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:43.880
I don't know whether to call it fate

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:47.930
or if the strength of your desire is
so intense that it overcomes everything.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:49.720
So, I'm changing tack.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:55.100
I'll take you outside of time
and eliminate your very existence.

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:02.400
Okay, come on, Daisuke.

00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:05.240
I've got a fully powered String Puppet
ready for you.

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:08.660
Isn't that your favorite toy?

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:13.250
What the...

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:14.460
What is that?

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:17.040
Daisuke.

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:21.170
This is the stage
where your attachment to this world ends.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.970
You're in perfect condition,
but I'll pulverize you

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:26.800
and eliminate all traces
of your existence.

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:27.970
Daisuke.

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:31.510
Milo, I'm going.

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:35.100
The destiny you told me,
that I will protect everyone,

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:37.480
I did my best and believed in it.

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:41.440
I can't ignore all that now.

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:44.360
I don't care if I don't return.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:47.610
This is my duty and my destiny.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:50.070
Milo,

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.540
thank you for everything.

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:02.090
That's the magic kiss
that my sister often gave me.

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:05.670
I will not forget you, Daisuke.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:07.840
So, don't you lose.

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:09.550
I know you can do it.

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:19.440
<i>Daisuke Dojima confirmed.</i>

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:25.440
Let's meet again in 2017.

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:28.070
Yes! You can bet on it!

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:45.800
Miss!

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.840
Where's Mr. Policeman?

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:50.550
He's all right.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:55.060
Listen to me, Daisuke. This is a prophecy.

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:59.390
The five of you will someday
find yourselves in terrible danger.

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:02.270
Only you will be able to protect them.

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:03.770
You.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:22.250
Daisuke, you have no idea
what it feels like to be a human

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:24.790
who can't get what they want.

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:28.090
I will take back what you've got.

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:32.760
I haven't gotten anything!

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:36.310
I'm only getting back the timeline
that everyone should live in.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:40.520
What?

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:53.360
Keisaku...

00:15:57.580 --> 00:16:02.210
Daisuke, why are you so rude?

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:07.210
Destiny is saying
that it doesn't need you.

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:10.470
<i>It says you don't have the ability
to fill the role of the main character.</i>

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:13.630
<i>I've decided to stop you!</i>

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:16.350
Don't push your beliefs on me!

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:17.720
Burst rounds!

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.720
Well, I'll be damned!

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:22.640
-You've fought well, Daisuke.
-Here he comes.

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:26.400
-My compliments!
-Your attacks are all the same!

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:29.280
<i>Audio data being transmitted
by the target.</i>

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:30.740
<i>Analyzing.</i>

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:33.400
<i>"Do it, Daisuke."</i>

00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:35.820
Keisaku!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:44.120
You fought hard too, Nicholas.

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:11.230
<i>Milo would probably get angry
if I break my promise.</i>

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:16.530
<i>What will everyone think
if I don't return?</i>

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:19.620
<i>I'm sorry, Keisaku.</i>

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:23.830
<i>I meant to save you, but...</i>

00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:28.210
<i>this is the best I could do.</i>

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:30.960
Bye.

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:37.720
-Jeez.
-What?

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:40.430
You sure are a pain in the neck.

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:43.270
We can finally talk, Daisuke.

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:45.020
How come you are here?

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:49.730
I've tried talking to you
several times already.

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:52.610
I get it now.

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:56.610
I always wondered what it was
that protected Daisuke.

00:17:57.200 --> 00:18:00.320
Keisaku, it was
your remaining consciousness.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:07.370
Here is where I completely eliminate
your consciousness.

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:10.540
Then I will completely establish
the true reality.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:15.590
You and I are one.

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:19.300
I can do the same things as you.

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:22.970
Gai, what's happening?

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:24.060
I don't know.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:26.520
But I can hear Keisaku's voice.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:28.770
He's saying, "Combine your strength!"

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:34.070
It's Daisuke! I'm sure of it!

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:38.150
Daisuke!

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:43.160
Don't do it, Keisaku.
We will both return to everyone!

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:47.080
Send my regards
to Marimari and everyone else.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:51.210
But maybe it's better not to say that
in this case.

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:53.500
Dammit! Why are you giving up?

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:55.840
This result is inevitable.

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:57.170
But you know, Daisuke,

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:58.760
it's the fate of your pitiful self

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:02.970
to wander through time-space
together with us.

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:05.850
Give it up, you pathetic jerk.

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:07.390
No.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:10.100
You know, Daisuke, you do have good luck.

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:20.240
You guys...

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:23.070
No!

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:26.080
I will drag this poor boy to hell with me!

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:35.500
No!

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:37.420
This won't be the last of me!

00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:41.050
I swear I'll be back someday!

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:52.440
Keisaku...

00:19:57.190 --> 00:19:59.240
Welcome back, Daisuke!

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:01.490
Thank goodness.

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:04.570
Let go of me, Lu.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:06.410
Daisuke.

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:08.790
You made it back.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:13.290
Keisaku saved me.

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:15.250
Right.

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:19.170
He connected us to you again.

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:21.380
Yes, he did.

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:24.590
Thank you, Keisaku.

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:31.770
NO TRESPASSING

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:35.810
<i>It's been three months
since we returned to 2017.</i>

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:39.280
<i>For several days, we were questioned
about what happened,</i>

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:41.530
<i>and our bodies were examined
inside and out.</i>

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:44.610
<i>They're hastily trying to determine</i>

00:20:44.860 --> 00:20:47.450
<i>the cause of the unprecedented
Shibuya Time-Space Disaster.</i>

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:51.910
<i>There's no way anyone can understand
what we have experienced.</i>

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:56.000
<i>But the people who saw the future</i>

00:20:56.540 --> 00:21:01.260
<i>are doing whatever they can
for the future that awaits us.</i>

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:04.510
<i>And for the people who died there as well.</i>

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:11.560
Daisuke!

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:13.730
We can finally see each other.

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:14.890
Yes.

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:17.100
Everyone looks good.

00:21:20.690 --> 00:21:22.690
We need to do our best from now on.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:24.450
That's right.

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:26.030
Yes.

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:29.490
I want to save Keisaku.

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:32.040
I'm sure he's alive somewhere.

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:39.080
"The end and the beginning.

00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:42.460
But the six of us

00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:44.760
need to be there,

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:48.720
even if a dreadful battle begins."

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:49.800
Isn't that...

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:52.100
That text was from Milo, wasn't it?

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:53.180
Yes.

00:21:53.890 --> 00:21:56.440
We'll see Milo and Keisaku again, right?

00:21:56.560 --> 00:21:57.390
Of course.

00:21:57.650 --> 00:22:01.480
Then, Milo is 25 or 26 years old now?

00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:05.860
Yes, I guess so.

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:12.280
<i>Gai, Lu, Marimari, Milo, and Keisaku.</i>

00:22:13.490 --> 00:22:18.170
<i>I'm sure that someday, the six of us
will talk fondly of this time together.</i>

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:20.630
<i>That's what I believe.</i>

00:22:21.790 --> 00:22:26.550
<i>That's because we're friends
who have formed irreplaceable bonds.</i>

00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:31.390
<i>Until that day comes,
my destiny isn't over.</i>

00:22:33.890 --> 00:22:35.220
<i>This is an urgent report.</i>

00:22:35.350 --> 00:22:40.350
<i>Moments ago, areas around the globe
suddenly disappeared.</i>

00:22:40.600 --> 00:22:45.530
<i>I repeat, areas around the globe
suddenly disappeared.</i>

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:47.240
<i>Since the Shibuya Time-Space Disaster...</i>

00:22:50.070 --> 00:22:52.070
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
